IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era25-types`
IMPORT `era25-rules`
IMPORT `era25-goal`

-- Independent tests: expected values come from independent-expectations.md,
-- derived from the Act before the encoding was read. Scenario numbers match.

GIVEN nn IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sickness facts`
mkNwe nn MEANS `Sickness facts` OF nn, Date 4 1 2027, 1

GIVEN dd IS A DATE, nn IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sickness facts`
mkInc dd nn MEANS `Sickness facts` OF 200, dd, nn

GIVEN ss IS A DATE, ee IS A DATE, aa IS A BOOLEAN, bb IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dismissal facts`
mkDis ss ee aa bb MEANS `Dismissal facts` OF ss, ee, aa, bb

GIVEN ss IS A DATE, ee IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
ordQ ss ee MEANS `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (mkDis ss ee FALSE FALSE)

GIVEN ss IS A DATE, ee IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
s642Q ss ee MEANS `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (mkDis ss ee TRUE FALSE)

GIVEN ss IS A DATE, ee IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
noPeriodQ ss ee MEANS `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (mkDis ss ee FALSE TRUE)

GIVEN kk IS A `Complaint kind`, dd IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
plain kk dd MEANS `the last day to present the complaint for` (`Complaint facts` OF kk, dd, NOTHING)

GIVEN kk IS A `Complaint kind`, dd IS A DATE, aa IS A DATE, bb IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
withEC kk dd aa bb MEANS
    `the last day to present the complaint for` (`Complaint facts` OF kk, dd, JUST (`Early conciliation` OF aa, bb))

-- SSP weekly rate (scenarios 1-9)
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 148.4375) EQUALS 118.75
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 200) EQUALS 118.75
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 1000) EQUALS 118.75
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 148) EQUALS 118.4
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 148.5) EQUALS 118.75
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 100) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 10) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 50) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (mkNwe 0) EQUALS 0

-- SSP start (scenarios 10-12)
#ASSERT `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` (mkInc (Date 4 1 2027) 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` (mkInc (Date 4 1 2027) 5) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` (mkInc (Date 11 1 2027) 3) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 1 2027)

-- Qualifying period (scenarios 13-31)
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 29 6 2027))
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 7 2027)
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 31 8 2027) (Date 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 31 8 2027) (Date 28 2 2028))
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 29 8 2027) (Date 28 2 2028)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 29 8 2027) (Date 27 2 2028))
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 29 8 2026) (Date 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 29 8 2026) (Date 27 2 2027))
#ASSERT ordQ (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 31 8 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 30 8 2027))
#ASSERT s642Q (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 31 1 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (s642Q (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 30 1 2027))
#ASSERT s642Q (Date 31 1 2027) (Date 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (s642Q (Date 31 1 2027) (Date 27 2 2027))
#ASSERT noPeriodQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 2 1 2027)
#ASSERT noPeriodQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (mkDis (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 2 1 2027) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (ordQ (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027))

